      "category": "Text",
      "text": "Whereas, Over these years certain common development procedures, techniques and expertise have evolved within the staff of the special development offices which are applicable to nearly all special development projects, including the use of special zoning districts to guide the growth and change of specific local commercial and commercial and residential areas; the designation, policy management and project management of specific urban renewal projects; sponsorship, designation and lease negotiations with public and private developers to implement specific development projects; the planning, preliminary design and implementation of major transit improvements, including subway stations and large scale transit malls; and",
